        <mxCell id="e12" value="and markdown-deck" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;strokeColor=#3A4A66;strokeWidth=1.3;fontColor=#3A4A66;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;endArrow=block;endFill=1;exitX=0.7;exitY=1;entryX=0.3;entryY=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="ap" target="md"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="406" y="636"/><mxPoint x="1228" y="636"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg" value="&lt;b&gt;Legend and rules&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot; color=&quot;#3a4a66&quot;&gt;Solid border: exists today. Dashed blue border: needed. Grey box: repository-local, or a tool that is not yet a skill. Solid arrow: hard dependency, the skill stops without it. Dashed arrow: reads, or composes.&lt;br&gt;1. A bundle depends only on bundles in the layers below it, and never on a repository above it. 2. A skill carries its method and its standards; where artefacts live is the repository's to declare. 3. The catalogue layer owns the definitions, the continuum; method bundles do not redefine them. 4. The scaffolding layer holds no layout of its own: it takes the house profile from the exemplar. 5. A solution keeps its architecture in a repository of its own (style A) or under docs/ of its own repository (style B); either way it is expressed with the continuum and checked by reconcile.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#D6DAE3;fontColor=#1B2A4A;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;arcSize=7;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="766" width="1360" height="118" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
